From 042b30b2e91795e8b3e56a8c8143c1e3e63e343d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 02:13:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] phase 6: security hardening + comprehensive SEO
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

SECURITY HARDENING

next.config.mjs — security headers on every route:
- Content-Security-Policy with self-only sources for a static site.
  script/style-src include 'unsafe-inline' (Next.js runtime + CSS Modules).
  frame-ancestors 'none', object-src 'none', upgrade-insecure-requests.
- Strict-Transport-Security: 2y with includeSubDomains + preload
- X-Frame-Options: DENY (backstops CSP frame-ancestors)
- X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
- Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
- Permissions-Policy: deny camera, mic, geolocation, payment, USB,
  MIDI, magnetometer, gyroscope, accelerometer, interest-cohort
- Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
- Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
- X-Powered-By header removed
- Long cache-control on _next/static hashed assets

public/robots.txt — allow /, disallow /dev/, points to sitemap
public/.well-known/security.txt — RFC 9116; contact, expires, canonical,
  policy pointer to /trust
SECURITY.md — vulnerability disclosure policy; safe-harbour language;
  documents recommended repo settings (branch protection, 2FA, signed
  commits, secret scanning, CodeQL)
.github/dependabot.yml — weekly npm + actions updates, minor/patch grouped
.github/workflows/ci.yml — TypeScript check, build, npm audit at
  high-severity threshold on every PR + push to main
public/site.webmanifest — corrected icon paths, added description/scope

SEO

Root layout (app/layout.tsx):
- metadataBase set to production URL
- Title template: '%s · Breachrr Security'
- Comprehensive keywords, publisher, category, format-detection blocks
- Explicit canonical, Open Graph, Twitter Card
- Robots: index+follow with googleBot: max-image-preview 'large'
- Icons: favicon variants + apple-touch-icon
- Web manifest link
- Viewport export with theme-color for light/dark
- Organization + ProfessionalService JSON-LD (Schema.org)
- WebSite JSON-LD

Homepage:
- Explicit metadata with alternates.canonical
- FAQPage JSON-LD from the 4 homepage questions — eligible for
  Google rich-result 'People also ask' surfaces
- ItemList JSON-LD enumerating the 6 service areas

Service detail pages (dynamic /services/[slug]):
- Dynamic metadata per service — title, description built from
  tagline+summary, canonical, OpenGraph, Twitter
- Service JSON-LD per page with hasOfferCatalog listing every
  specific service under that category
- BreadcrumbList JSON-LD (Home → Services → [Category])

Approach, Services overview, Work, Contact, Trust:
- Enhanced metadata with alternates.canonical, OG, Twitter

Terms + Privacy pages:
- robots: index=false (legal boilerplate shouldn't compete in SEO)
- Canonical URL still set

Dev page:
- robots: index=false, follow=false, nocache=true (internal only)

app/sitemap.ts — Next.js sitemap primitive; enumerates all 8 static
  routes + 6 dynamic service routes with priority + changeFrequency.
  Available at /sitemap.xml.

app/not-found.tsx + not-found.module.css — proper 404 inside site chrome
  with four recovery links (Home / Approach / Services / Contact).
  Returns HTTP 404. Matches brand visual language.

app/opengraph-image.tsx — dynamic 1200x630 OG image generated at edge.
  Paper canvas + hairline grid + wordmark with moss middle-dot + slogan
  + booking indicator. Referenced from Twitter + OpenGraph metadata.
